exact.text:
Let $ k \geq 14 $ be an integer, and let $ q $ be the largest prime less than $ k $, with $ q \geq 3k/4 $. Let $ n $ be a composite number. Prove:
\na. if $ n = 2q $, then $ n $ does not divide $ (n - k)! $;
\nb. if $ n > 2q $, then $ n $ divides $ (n - k)! $.

style.text:
Let $m \geq 14$ be an integer, and let $q_{m}$ be the largest prime less than $m$. You may assume that $q_{m} \geq 3m/4$. Let $a$ be a composite integer. Prove: 
\na. if $a = 2q_{m}$, then $a$ does not divide $(a-m)!$;
\nb. if $a > 2q_{m}$, then $a$ divides $(a-m)!$.

