(1) $g_i(x)$ is even and $g_i(x+\pi) = g_i(x)$ for all $x$;

(2) $g(x) = g_1(x) + g_2(x)\cos x + g_3(x)\sin x + g_4(x)\sin 2x$ for all $x$.

exact.text:
Let $P$ be a $3 \times 9$ matrix of nonnegative entries such that:
(1) Each row contains distinct elements;
(2) For each of the first six columns, the sum of the two entries is $1$;
(3) The last entry in each row is zero: $x_{17} = x_{28} = x_{39} = 0$;
(4) The remaining three columns (columns 7, 8, 9) contain values strictly greater than $1$.
Let $S$ denote the submatrix formed by the first three columns of $P$. Then for any column vector $[x_{1k}, x_{2k}, x_{3k}]$ in $P$, there is an index $i \in \{1, 2, 3\}$ for which $x_{ik} \le u_i$, where $u_i = \min\{x_{i1}, x_{i2}, x_{i3}\}$.

paraphrase.text:
Let $ n $ be an integer greater than or equal to 2. Determine the minimal positive integer $ m $ such that there exist $ n^2 $ distinct positive real numbers $ a_{i,j} $ ($ 1 \le i, j \le n $) satisfying the following:
(1) For each $ i, j $,
$$
 a_{i,j} = \max\{a_{i,1}, a_{i,2}, \dots, a_{i,j}\} \text{ or}
$$
$$
 a_{i,j} = \max\{a_{1,j}, a_{2,j}, \dots, a_{i,j}\};
$$
(2) For each row $ i $, the number of columns $ k $ for which $ a_{i,k} = \max\{a_{i,1}, a_{i,2}, \dots, a_{i,k}\} $ is at most $ m $;
(3) For each column $ j $, the number of rows $ k $ for which $ a_{k,j} = \max\{a_{1,j}, a_{2,j}, \dots, a_{k,j}\} $ is at most $ m $.

style.text:
Given integer $ n \ge 2 $. Determine the smallest positive integer $ m $ for which it is possible to assign $ n^2 $ distinct positive real numbers $ a_{r,s} $ ($ 1 \le r, s \le n $) such that:
(1) For each $ r, s $, $ a_{r,s} $ is either the maximum of its row $ a_{r,1}, a_{r,2}, \dots, a_{r,s} $ or the maximum of its column $ a_{1,s}, a_{2,s}, \dots, a_{r,s} $;
(2) In every row $ r $, there are at most $ m $ entries that are the maximum of their prefix in the row;
(3) In every column $ s $, there are at most $ m $ entries that are the maximum of their prefix in the column.

exact.text:
Sei $P$ die Menge aller Tupel $(p, q)$ mit $p, q \in \mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0}$. Bestimme alle Funktionen $f: P \rightarrow \mathrm{IR}$, welche die folgende Bedingung erfüllen:
$$\nf(p, q)=\left\{\begin{array}{c}
0 \quad \text{falls } p q = 0 \\
1+\frac{1}{2} f(p+1, q-1)+\frac{1}{2} f(p-1, q+1) \text{ sonst }
\end{array} .\right.
$$

paraphrase.text:
Sei $P$ die Menge aller Paare $(a, b)$ mit nichtnegativen ganzen Zahlen $a$ und $b$. Finde alle Funktionen $g: P \rightarrow \mathrm{IR}$, die die folgende Bedingung erfüllen:
$$\ng(a, b)=\left\{\begin{array}{c}
0 \quad \text{ wenn } ab=0 \\
1+\frac{1}{2} g(a+1, b-1)+\frac{1}{2} g(a-1, b+1) \text{ sonst }
\end{array} .\right.
$$

