exact.text:
Numbers from $2$ to $99$ are written on the board. In each move, we can either:
\ni. Remove two numbers $a$ and $a+10$ if both are still on the board and $2 \le a \le 89$;
\nii. Remove two numbers $a$ and $a+1$ if both are still on the board, $2 \le a \le 98$, and $10 \nmid a$;

What is the maximum number of numbers that can be removed from the board using these operations?

paraphrase.text:
