\ni. Pick an integer $a$, $2 \le a \le 89$, and if both $a$ and $a + 10$ are still on the board, remove both;
\nii. Pick an integer $b$, $2 \le b \le 98$, not divisible by $10$, and if both $b$ and $b + 1$ are still on the board, remove both;

What is the maximum number of numbers that can be removed from the board using these operations?

style.text:
