\ni. Pick an integer $a$, $2 \le a \le 89$ and if both $a$ and $a+10$ are still on the board, remove both;
\nii. Pick an integer $a$, $2 \le a \le 98$, not divisible by $10$, and if both $a$ and $a+1$ are still on the board, remove both;

What is the maximum number of integers that can be erased from the board using these operations?

