Let $\mathbb{Z}^*$ denote the set of all nonzero integers and $\mathbb{N}_0$ the set of all nonnegative integers. Determine all functions $f:\mathbb{Z}^* \to \mathbb{N}_0$ satisfying:

(1) For all $x,y \in \mathbb{Z}^*$ with $x+y \in \mathbb{Z}^*$, it holds that $f(x+y) \ge \min\{f(x),f(y)\}$;

(2) For all $x,y \in \mathbb{Z}^*$, it holds that $f(xy) = f(x)+f(y)$.

